--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution: BBP Pairings
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ainalrami contains work derived from BBP Pairings
(https://github.com/BieremaBoyzProgramming/bbpPairings),
Copyright 2016-2026 Jeremy Bierema, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

No BBP Pairings source code is reproduced here. Ainalrami is written in
Elixir and BBP Pairings in C++, so nothing was copied verbatim. What was
taken is the ALGORITHM AND CONTROL FLOW of one component, read directly
from the BBP Pairings source while writing the Elixir equivalent, with
the originating file and line numbers cited inline throughout. Stating
that plainly here rather than leaving it to be inferred:

  * lib/ainalrami/pairing.ex — the FIDE Dutch-system bracket cascade,
    ported stage for stage from src/swisssystems/dutch.cpp, including the
    C1-C21 criteria encoding, the bootstrap bye-assignee matching, the
    per-bracket refinement stages and the candidate-ordering (addend)
    passes.

Changes made relative to BBP Pairings, as required by section 4(b) of the
Apache License 2.0: the code is a reimplementation in a different language and is not
a line-for-line translation. Where BBP Pairings re-solves after the refinement
stages 4, 7 and 8 rewrite weights, Ainalrami.Pairing first tries to absorb
the change by moving dual variables, and re-solves only when that does
not leave the matching optimal.
Ainalrami.Pairing differs in its peek/window handling and in several
places where a non-literal reading is argued in the code comments rather
than copied. Individual deviations are documented at their call sites and
in docs/engineering-log.md.

The following parts of Ainalrami are NOT derived from BBP Pairings:
lib/ainalrami/trf.ex implements FIDE's published TRF16 specification
(C.04 Annex 2) and was adapted from the author's own OpenPairings
project; lib/ainalrami/sequence.ex implements Article 4 of C.04.3 (2026)
directly from the regulations; lib/ainalrami/weighted_matching.ex is a
maximum-weight matching written for this project from the published
literature (Edmonds 1965; Galil 1986), and replaced in full the earlier
module that was derived from BBP Pairings' matcher; lib/ainalrami/cli.ex,
generator.ex, matching.ex and log.ex are original work.

